<title>UK: Invesco new shares to start dealing Feb 27.</title>
<headline>Invesco new shares to start dealing Feb 27.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>British investment management company Invesco Plc said on Wednesday that dealing in the shares from its one-for-five rights issue of convertible unsecured loan stock would begin on February 27.</p>
<p>Invesco also said its previously-announced merger with U.S. group AIM Management Group Inc. was expected to be completed by February 28. Earlier this month Invesco said it received loan commitments from a syndicate of banks allowing it to complete the merger.</p>
<p>The rights issue was priced at 220p per unit of convertible loan stock. The conversion of the 54,269,108 units of loan stock will take place on February 26.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
